{"full":"elewah/RadViz-Plotly","name":"RadViz-Plotly","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":7,"forks":0,"created":"2020-08-04T00:13:51Z","updated":"2026-03-02T03:45:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/elewah/RadViz-Plotly/blob/master/iframe_figures/BreastCancer_2D_RadViz.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:17:56.464Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:17:56.464Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:17:56.464Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:56.212Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:17:56.464Z","stars":7,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Latest Release Examples PyPI Downloads License","RadViz-Plotly is an open-source Python package designed for data scientists to create 2D and 3D Radial Visualization (RadViz) plots for high-dimensional datasets. These visualizations provide a comprehensive view of data distribution across dimensions, enabling better understanding and discovery of hidden insights. The package leverages the powerful interactive tools of the Plotly library.","RadViz-Plotly was developed by a research group at the IoT Lab, Ontario Tech University. It provides tools for creating 2D and 3D Radial Visualizations, enabling data scientists to explore high-dimensional datasets interactively."],"features":["2DRadViz: Generates 2D Radial Visualizations.","3DRadViz: Creates 3D Radial Visualizations.","3DRadViz with Attribute Sorting: Creates 3D Radial Visualizations with intelligent attribute sorting based on correlation analysis.","Interactive Visualizations: Zoom, filter labels, and rotate 3D graphs.","Correlation-Based Grouping: Automatically groups highly correlated attributes and separates negatively correlated ones."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elewah/RadViz-Plotly/blob/master/README.md","fingerp